# DrafterLeftovers-2b (lane DrafterLeftovers, 2026-10-30; HuntDrafter F6): DFlash2 taps reach the drafter unbuilt.
# A prompt chunk's taps were concatenated whole (torch.cat over the 5 tap layers: 4,096 x 20,480 bf16 = 168 MB written,
# then read again by the update's copies) though the update launches only the rows it keeps (HuntDrafter-1's
# ring_skip: the last 34 x 64 of 4,096; TF_GLM_DRAFT_SKIP's WindowTaps: the rows near a read point). Now the producers
# (decode.prefill_chunk / prefill_chunk_steps via Engine.tap_view, multi_prefill.prefill_pieces / prefill_piece_steps,
# and BatchedVerify.forward's round windows) hand a dflash2.TapRows view of the forward's per-layer buffers; the update
# copies each launch's rows straight into its input (copy_taps: torch.cat(out=) of the row slices), so dropped rows are
# never copied and kept rows are copied once. The same bytes land in tap_in: bit-identical ring rows, device ends,
# context ends and candidates (GPU test against the base tree's digests). TapRows is read before the next forward on
# those buffers: every update launches its copies before returning, on the same stream.
# Applies with `patch -p0` in the folder holding tensorfold/, after DrafterLeftovers-1.
# 2b: rebased onto stack/all6's base (RoundGraphs' lazy verify.WindowTaps: its items are now TapRows views).
